",,True,-1,"To solve this problem, I need to prove that a certain type of closed path (a `(p.trans q).trans r`) is equivalent to a specific reparametrization of the concatenated paths `p.trans (q.trans r)`. The proof requires showing that both paths are equal pointwise by reparametrizing the two paths and then using properties of continuous functions and path homotopies to show that the resulting paths are homotopic and eventually identical.

